  "historicalDocumentEvidencePopulations": {
    "ticket-report": {
      "grammar": "historical-document-evidence-v1",
      "directoryPattern": "**/.🧬semio/🦑️repo/🎫️tickets/🎆️[0-9][0-9]/🌙️[0-9][0-9]/☀️[0-9][0-9]/*/**",
      "leafPattern": "^📓️.+\\.md$",
      "reason": "A 📓️-slugged file under a ticket directory is a narrative record of what was true when it was written, per CLAUDE.md's own ticket protocol (research/summary markdown). Document kind, not the owning ticket's open/closed lifecycle status, is the discriminator: rewriting it would falsify the record it keeps, and blocking on its bare prose would freeze the whole repository on prose in any ticket, open or closed. The whole document is therefore excluded from reference-candidate scanning unconditionally."
    },
    "ticket-workspace": {
      "grammar": "historical-document-evidence-v1",
      "directoryPattern": "**/.🧬semio/🦑️repo/🎫️tickets/🎆️[0-9][0-9]/🌙️[0-9][0-9]/☀️[0-9][0-9]/*/**",
      "leafPattern": "^.+$",
      "reason": "Any descendant of a ticket root, at any nesting depth, that is not itself a registered fixedFilenameContracts file is ticket workspace — evidence snapshots (e.g. *.pre-patch.rs), scratch scripts, census/log output, working notes (📌️*.md), and their own nested subfolders (e.g. 📥️worker-bootstrap/, 🧪️run-*/) — never a live reference. Depth was never the safety property: it is exempted only when it is not itself a fixedFilenameContracts match AND no ancestor directory up to the ticket root owns a package-root manifest (Cargo.toml/package.json/go.mod/…, any fixedFilenameContracts entry with scope.kind===\"package-root\"); a ticket-embedded package, and any fixed-filename contract file wherever it sits (e.g. 📜️script.ts, matched by root-script's own **/📜️script.ts pattern regardless of location), keeps its normal live-reference treatment."
    },
    "cursor-plan-snapshot": {
      "grammar": "historical-document-evidence-v1",
      "directoryPattern": ".cursor/plans/*",
      "leafPattern": "^.+\\.plan\\.md$",
      "reason": "Cursor IDE plan snapshots are historical planning narrative authored by a separate tool with no ticket-lifecycle concept; they are never live references and are unconditionally excluded from reference-candidate scanning."
    },
    "dev-prompt-log": {
      "grammar": "historical-document-evidence-v1",
      "directoryPattern": "**/.🧬semio/🦑️repo/💬️prompts/**",
      "leafPattern": "^.+\\.md$",
      "reason": "Each file under 💬️prompts/ is one developer's own running prompt-log transcript — narrative of what was asked and done at the time, per the same argument that already exempts 📓️ ticket reports and Cursor plan snapshots: rewriting a transcript falsifies the historical record it keeps, and blocking a rename on a bare path token quoted somewhere in a dev's prompt history would freeze the whole repository on prose nobody intends to keep in sync. Unlike ticket-report this population carries no 📓️ prefix and no ticket-lifecycle concept at all — the directory itself (one markdown file per developer, e.g. 🐙️ueli.md, 🐳️kinan.md, 🦢️niloufar.md) is the whole population, discriminated purely by location. Still subject to both existing negatives: never exempts a fixedFilenameContracts match, and never exempts a path inside a directory (up to 💬️prompts/ itself) that owns a package-root manifest."
    }
  },
